  "result": "Fixed: `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now clamps to the value just inside the range.\n\nThe cause was in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. For an open bound it returned `bound - dir`, which steps the wrong way. With `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)`, the input `0` came back as `-1`, outside the range. It now returns `bound + dir`, so `0` becomes `1` and `5` with `max_open=True` becomes `4`.\n\nI added four cases to `tests/test_types.py` covering both open bounds, including values past the far end. `tests/test_types.py` passes (45 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't re-run the new cases against the unfixed code, but the old formula gives `-1` for the `0` case, so they would have failed before.\n\nI didn't add a changelog entry. The issue was only in `IntRange`, since `FloatRange` already rejects clamping with open bounds.",
